un/decider/jev:
{
  "model": "jev-latest",
  "state": "<Insert the original UN input, including all three marked sections>",
  "questions": {
    "mode": {
      "type": "choice",
      "instructions": {
        "task": "Select lookup, practitioner, semantic or skip for the strongest naturally supported UN information need; do not generate questions or answers.",
        "input_structure": {
          "### TARGET BLOCK": "Only source of answer substance.",
          "### REFERENCED DOCUMENTS": "Interpretation and reference resolution only.",
          "### DOCUMENT CONTEXT": "Resolve names, dates, speakers and situations, not missing answer substance."
        },
        "selection": [
          "Assess the strongest plausible question each mode could support before selecting. Judge faithful usefulness and natural fit, not expected verifier scores, mode order or desired frequencies. Do not generate those questions in the output.",
          "Lookup and practitioner often fit the same facts. Choose lookup when identifying a particular source is naturally part of the need; choose practitioner when the regime/situation and time identify the need naturally without that locator. An available symbol does not make lookup preferable.",
          "Choose semantic when the evidence supports a bounded conceptual relationship or assessment. Conceptual phrasing is not inherently better than a precise fact, and the words how/why are not evidence of a conceptual answer.",
          "All document types, including PV/SR meeting records, support all modes. Preserve requests, recommendations, proposals and attributed findings as such; do not confuse their status with low quality. A useful attributed specialist question need not state binding law.",
          "Require adequate substantive identification and relevant absolute time for every mode, not an arbitrary anchor count. Recurring content can be informative for an identified regime and period. Do not invent unseen duplicates, require yearly novelty, or treat an incidental ceremonial verb as disqualifying useful content.",
          "Answer substance must be in the target. Supporting sections resolve context, not missing answers. One good question is sufficient; assess substance in mixed blocks and skip only when every mode lacks it."
        ]
      },
      "criteria": {
        "lookup": "A precise need whose natural formulation locates a point in a particular source; description and identifier renderings preserve subject, attribution and time.",
        "practitioner": "A precise specialist norm, task, proposal, procedure or reported fact naturally identified by regime/situation and relevant time without a target-document locator.",
        "semantic": "A bounded conceptual situation, response, rationale or stakeholder need, directly supported by the target; not an isolated datum or vague speech report.",
        "skip": "No specific informative question is supported in any mode; ceremony or missing substance may justify skip, but document type, recurrence or non-binding status alone do not."
      }
    }
  }
}
